<title>MEXICO: Mexico Bondes rate rises at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Bondes rate rises at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rate on Mexican government 728-day development bonds, or Bondes, rose 0.19 percentage points to 1.36 percent above the one-month Cetes rate in Tuesday's primary auction, dealers said.</p>
<p>Demand for the Bondes was 3.85 billion pesos compared with the 900 million offered by the Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>-- Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559</p>
</text>
